# A Wi-Fi device that appears starts segno-wifi-retry (#1963).
#
# segno-wifi-ctl manages a USB Wi-Fi adapter whenever one is plugged in. One
# plugged in while the console runs would otherwise leave the link on wlan0
# while the Network page read the idle adapter. The retry finds the adapter
# disconnected and brings a saved network up on it, pinning the profile there;
# it holds off while the app performs and stands down when the radio is off.
# At boot the same event only asks for a unit multi-user.target already
# starts. TAG+="systemd" and SYSTEMD_WANTS, as in 98-segno-usb-storage.rules:
# the unit is started by systemd, not by a RUN program udev would kill.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="wlan", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="segno-wifi-retry.service"
